{"A01": "Complete your campus network login below 👇. Rest assured, our app never touches, saves, or uploads your plaintext password 🔒💖!", "A02": "Called up your default browser to open the login page 🚀!", "A03": "Held off on auto-opening 🛡️: we noticed this URL isn't under JLU's official jlu.edu.cn domain 🧐", "A04": "Once you've signed in through your browser 🌐, remember to hop back here and click \"I've Logged In\" 🙋‍♂️! Our app never even sees your plaintext password during the whole process 🛡️✨!", "A05": "Please triple-check that you're connected to the real JLU.WIFI or JLU.PC and that the URL looks legit before proceeding ⚠️🕵️‍♂️✨!", "A06": "Reopen Login Page 🔄", "A07": "I've verified it—open this page anyway 🦸‍♂️", "A08": "Never mind, cancel ✖️", "A09": "I've Logged In! 🎉", "A10": "Heads up! 🚨 This login page URL doesn't end with jlu.edu.cn 🧐", "A11": "Only proceed if you're 100% sure you're connected to the official JLU.WIFI / JLU.PC campus Wi-Fi ⚠️;", "A12": "If you're on a sketchy network with a weird name, never type your precious campus account or password into it 🙅‍♂️🛡️!", "A13": "Aww 😭, campus network authentication hasn't gone through yet", "A14": "Test Again 🔄", "A15": "If you're off-campus right now (e.g., on a phone hotspot or home Wi-Fi 🏠), you'll need WebVPN to reach internal university sites 💡🌉; if you're sitting in your dorm plugged into Ethernet, hit Retry Auth first 🔄. Clicking the button below opens WebVPN and copies your username to the clipboard automatically 📋✨!", "A16": "Open JLU WebVPN 🌉", "A17": "Copy Password 🔑", "A18": "Easy 3-step combo 🐾: Once the page loads, pick \"JLU Pass / Unified Auth\" under Faculty & Student Login 👉 Paste your username (already copied for you 📋!) 👉 Enter your password 👉 Come back here and hit \"Test Again\" 🎉!", "A19": "Username copied for you ✅: {…} ✨", "A20": "You haven't saved a username yet 🙈—head over to \"Settings\" and fill it in first ✍️!", "A21": "No password saved on this Mac yet 🤔—save it in \"Settings\" first 💾!", "A22": "Password copied! 🔐 To protect your privacy, we'll clear it from your clipboard automatically in 60 seconds ⏱️🛡️", "A23": "Campus Welcome Portal 🏫", "A24": "The university portal page (that welcome/bulletin screen that pops up after connecting) opens straight in your default system browser 🌐✨.", "A25": "We skip bundling a heavy web view inside our lightweight app 🛡️, keeping memory usage tiny and completely avoiding web-rendering crashes 🍃✨!", "A26": "Open in Browser 🚀", "A27": "Haven't captured a portal URL yet 📭", "A28": "Connect to the campus network once (or let the unauthenticated captive portal intercept a probe 🚧), and we'll jot down the portal address automatically 💡📝✨!", "A29": "Copy magic command to disable macOS auto-popup window 📋🪄", "B101": "Not connected yet 😴", "B102": "You're inside the campus gates 🚶‍♂️, but haven't swiped your card at the turnstile yet 🪪.", "B103": "Tap \"Connect / Log In\" below 👇 and we'll swipe you right through in a flash 🚀✨!", "B104": "Connecting at full speed 🏃‍♂️…", "B105": "Checking your ID with the campus gateway guard 🪪—like the gatekeeper squinting at your student card 👀, it usually takes just a second or two ⏱️✨!", "B106": "Rock-Solid Connected! 🎉", "B107": "JLU Gate is standing guard over your connection 24/7 🛡️—go surf the web to your heart's content 🏄‍♂️💖!", "B108": "Connected 🤝 (Official client is currently in the driver's seat)", "B109": "The official Dr.Com client is holding onto the auth channel right now 🏠 (it grabbed the port first),but the great news is your internet is wide open and ready to roll 🌐✨!", "B110": "Want to hand the baton over to the lighter, snappier JLU Gate? 🔄 Quit the official client first 👋,then click \"Connect\" right here ✨!", "B111": "Official client is hogging the line, but isn't connected yet 🚧🙈", "B112": "The official client has a death grip on the authentication port, yet hasn't actually logged you in 📞—like someone camping inside a phone booth without dialing 😅💦!", "B113": "Completely quit the official Dr.Com client first 👉 (and check Activity Monitor for its sneaky background process DrClientNS 🧹), then hit \"Connect\" here to bring your network back to life 🚀!", "B114": "Patiently waiting for network hardware ⏳…", "B115": "Your Mac doesn't have an active Ethernet link or IP address yet 🚗—like a sports car waiting to merge onto the highway on-ramp 🛣️.", "B116": "Plug your cable in snug 🔌 (or make sure the adapter has an IP), and we'll automatically hit the gas the moment the road opens up 🏃‍♂️✨!", "B117": "Aww, couldn't connect 😭", "B118": "We gave it our best shot 🧗‍♂️, but hit a roadblock at the campus gateway 🚧.", "B119": "Don't sweat it 👇! Check the friendly tips below, tweak the setting, and hit \"Retry\" to breeze right through 💪✨!", "B120": "The official campus client beat us to the dedicated auth hotline 📞 (UDP port 61440), so our call can't get through 🙈.", "B121": "Web authentication needs your browser to step in 🌐: once the login page pops up and you sign in, remember to click \"I've Logged In\" back here 🙋‍♂️✨!", "B122": "Loopback Interface 🔄 (Your Mac talking to itself 🗣️)", "B123": "Built into the macOS kernel 🧠", "B124": "127.0.0.1 is strictly for passing notes inside your own Mac 🏠—packets here never travel down an external cable 🔒.", "B125": "Conjured up by a VPN or proxy app 🪄 (couldn't catch which background process owns it right now 🕵️‍♂️)", "B126": "Created by \"{…}\" 🪄", "B127": "Virtual Tunnel Interface 🚇 (Encrypted Tunnel)", "B128": "Your proxy app uses this as the main front door for internet traffic 🚪; if it accidentally scoops up the campus subnet too, your auth packets will get lost on the way to the university gateway 🚨!", "B129": "Mystery Apple Internal Interface 🍎", "B130": "Built into macOS / Apple Silicon ⚙️ (not a physical port you can plug a cable into 🙅‍♂️)", "B131": "Used strictly for Apple's behind-the-scenes magic 📱 (like Continuity, AirDrop, or Apple Watch Unlock ✨)—nothing to do with campus internet browsing 🏖️.", "B132": "AirDrop / AirPlay Direct Wireless Channel ✈️", "B133": "Apple-exclusive peer-to-peer wireless link 📡 (not used for general web browsing)", "B134": "Handles photo sharing and screen mirroring with nearby iPhones and iPads 🤝, leaving heavy web traffic to your main network card ✨.", "B135": "Thunderbolt Bridge ⚡", "B136": "Created automatically by macOS 🔗 (only used when linking two Macs directly together with a Thunderbolt cable 💻⚡💻)", "B137": "Sits idle 99% of the time 💤; if it ever shows up as your default outbound route, your macOS Network Service Order got scrambled 😵‍💫!", "B138": "Wi-Fi (Wireless LAN) 📡", "B139": "Your Mac's built-in wireless card 💻 (or a portable Wi-Fi adapter ✨)", "B140": "Handles browser authentication on JLU.WIFI 🌐 and runs the Dr.Com protocol when you're on JLU.PC 🏃‍♂️✨!", "B141": "USB Ethernet Adapter 🔌", "B142": "External Ethernet port on a USB dongle or hub (Heads up: switching USB ports can change its enX name 🎭, so we track it by its permanent MAC address 🎯!)", "B143": "No IPv4 address yet ⚠️: you probably just plugged it in and haven't configured your static campus IP in System Settings yet 📝.", "B144": "Swapping USB ports or adapters often changes the system interface name 💡, but JLU only checks your registered MAC address—so make sure your MAC matches 🪪✨!", "B145": "Thunderbolt Ethernet Adapter ⚡", "B146": "High-speed built-in or external Ethernet adapter 🔌", "B147": "Ethernet port on a high-end Thunderbolt dock ⚡", "B148": "Built-in Ethernet port or dock Ethernet interface 💻", "B149": "No IPv4 address yet ⚠️: make sure the cable is clicked in tight and your static campus IP is configured before authenticating 🛠️✨!", "B150": "Your trusty workhorse for wired surfing 📌: just make sure the IP / Mask / Gateway match your official registration slip to the letter 📋✨!", "B151": "Wired Ethernet Adapter 🔌", "B152": "Standard macOS network interface 🌐", "B153": "Looking sharp and ready for campus authentication anytime ✅🚀!", "B154": "Other System Interface 🧩", "B155": "Built into low-level system services ⚙️", "B156": "Completely unrelated to everyday web browsing 🍃—safe to ignore 😎.", "B157": "Locked onto \"{…}\" as your chosen champion 🔒🎯!", "B158": "You haven't entered a Registered MAC yet 🤖: we'll smartly pick the best available adapter for you (giving priority to rock-solid Wired Ethernet 🔌✨).", "B159": "Searched top to bottom 😱, but none of your network cards match the MAC registered with JLU {…} (found on this Mac: {…}). Plug back in your registered dongle/dock, or update your MAC on the Campus Self-Service Portal 🏫✍️!", "B160": "Bullseye! 🎯 Locked onto target interface by MAC address: {…} ({…}) ✨!", "B161": "Whoa 👯‍♂️! Multiple interfaces share the registered MAC address {…}! To avoid picking the wrong one, please select your preferred adapter manually below 👇✨.", "B201": "Oops 🙈, {…} doesn't look like a valid IPv4 address (it should be four numbers separated by three dots 🔢)", "B202": "Subnet mask bits aren't contiguous 📏: {…} (it usually looks like 255.255.255.0 ✨)", "B203": "Gateway {…} wandered off into the wrong neighborhood 🚧—it's not inside your {…}/{…} subnet 🏘️!", "B204": "Your gateway address can't be identical to your own local IP ({…}) 👯‍♂️—packets mailed to yourself will never leave the room 🚪💦!", "B205": "MAC address format looks a bit off 🪪: {…} (should be 6 pairs of hex characters, like a1:b2:c3:d4:e5:f6 ✨)", "B206": "Gateway 🚪", "B207": "Couldn't read how this interface is configured 🙈. Please copy your static IP straight from your campus registration slip 📝—never use a temporary DHCP address 🙅‍♂️!", "B208": "This adapter is currently in {…} mode ⚠️, wearing a temporary auto-assigned address that won't work as a static IP 🙅‍♂️. Please copy the fixed numbers from your registration slip instead ✍️!", "B209": "Set to manual configuration in macOS 🤔, but this adapter doesn't have an IPv4 address assigned to it yet 📭.", "B210": "Sweet! 🎉 This adapter is already in manual static mode. The numbers below are what your Mac is actively using right now—feel free to grab them (and give your registration slip a quick glance just to be 100% sure 👀✨)!", "B211": "Please enter the username prefix before @{…} in your JLU email ✍️✨.", "B212": "Usernames can only contain letters and numbers 🔤 (just enter the prefix before @, not the full email address 🙅‍♂️✨).", "B213": "Ooh, looks like a faculty/staff account 👨‍🏫! The format is your full pinyin name (e.g.,zhangshanwu), with a number suffix if someone shares your name—use your exact email prefix 📧.Note: Enter your JLU Pass (Unified Identity Auth) password here 🔑✨!", "B214": "Hey there, fellow student 🎓! Student usernames follow the pattern: Full Surname Pinyin + Given Name Initials + 4 digits (2-digit major code + 2-digit enrollment year), like zhangcyy2122 🌰✨.", "B215": "Student account recognized! 🎒 Major code {…}, Class of 20{…} 🎉! Remember: enter your JLU Pass (Unified Identity Auth) password here 🔑✨!", "B216": "Quick reminder 💡! Your username is the prefix before @{…} in your JLU email, and the password is your everyday JLU Pass (Unified Identity Auth) password 🔑: · 🎓 Students: Surname Pinyin + Given Name Initials + 4 digits (2-digit major + 2-digit year), e.g., zhangcyy2122; · 👨‍🏫 Faculty & Staff: Full name in Pinyin, e.g., zhangshanwu (use your exact email prefix if it includes a number suffix ✨).", "B301": "Pure Direct Connection 🍃 (No proxy active)", "B302": "Proxy is steering public traffic 🦸‍♂️ (while campus intranet traffic stays on the direct lane 🛣️✨)", "B303": "Global Proxy Mode 🌍 (Even campus intranet traffic got scooped up by your proxy 🚨)", "B304": "TUN virtual adapter is on 🚇, but hasn't taken over the default route yet 💤", "B305": "Too foggy to tell right now 🤔", "B306": "Not configured yet ⚪", "B307": "Rule Mode ⚖️ (Smart split-tunneling by rules ✨)", "B308": "Global Mode 🌍 (All traffic goes through proxy)", "B309": "Direct Mode 🛣️", "B310": "Current Scenario 🎬", "B311": "(Actually detected 🕵️‍♂️: {…})", "B312": "All network traffic walks straight out your physical adapter{…} 🍃—zero chance of a proxy swallowing your campus auth packets. Rock solid 🛡️✨!", "B313": "Public internet traffic gets escorted by your proxy ✈️, while JLU campus traffic marches straight out via {…}{…} ⚖️—teamwork makes the dream work 🤝✨!", "B314": "Fun fact 💡: Smart clients like Shadowrocket or Clash usually bypass LAN and campus subnets under the hood even when you flip the switch to \"Global\" mode 🛣️—", "B315": "so checking the routing table alone can't tell whether you clicked \"Global\" or \"Rule.\" Either way, as long as our auth packets don't take a detour, that's a huge win 🎉✨!", "B316": "Uh-oh 🚨, even JLU's internal campus subnet got scooped up by your virtual adapter{…}! That means your login packets have to loop through your proxy app's belly before heading out 🌀—whether login succeeds depends entirely on how steady that detour is:", "B317": "If your proxy is snappy with near-zero latency and no packet loss ⏱️, authentication will still sneak through ✌️; but the moment the proxy stutters or queues up, auth and keep-alive heartbeats time out and the campus server drops your connection 😭💦!", "B318": "We see a TUN virtual adapter in macOS 🚇, but it hasn't grabbed the default route steering wheel yet{…}—either your routing rules didn't match, or the proxy master switch isn't fully engaged 🤔.", "B319": "Couldn't read the system routing table this time 🙈, so we can't make the call 🤷‍♂️.", "B320": "Everything looks awesome right now 👍—no changes needed! When you want to explore the wider web 🌍, just flip Shadowrocket/Clash to \"Rule (Config)\" or \"Global (Proxy)\" mode anytime ✨.", "B321": "This split-tunnel setup is the absolute sweet spot for campus authentication 💖: leave it right as it is! If you ever drop offline out of the blue, just check that your proxy rules didn't accidentally swallow 10.0.0.0/8 🕵️‍♂️✨.", "B322": "In Global mode 🛠️, we recommend clicking \"Test Auth Channel\" first ⏱️: if going through the proxy is way slower than direct or drops packets 🐢, switch your proxy to \"Rule (Config)\" mode and add a direct rule for 10.0.0.0/8 (e.g., IP-CIDR,10.0.0.0/8,DIRECT in Clash) ✍️! If latency stays lightning-fast,Global mode works fine in a pinch—just slightly more prone to occasional drops 🤏✨.", "B323": "If you meant to route traffic through your proxy 🤔, double-check that your Shadowrocket/Clash master switch is on and your rules are loaded; if you just want a chill campus connection, you're already good to go 🍃✨!", "B324": "Hop over to the \"Network Details\" tab 🔄 and hit Re-detect to take a fresh look 🔍✨!", "B325": "DNS Lookup Failed 📖💥 (Couldn't find the IP address for this domain 🙈)", "B326": "Connection Failed 🔌💥 (Knocked on the server's door, nobody answered 🚪)", "B327": "TLS Handshake Rejected 🔒💥", "B328": "Server turned down our request 🙅‍♂️", "B329": "Timed out waiting for a reply ⏱️🥀", "B330": "Campus Intranet Only 🏫", "B331": "Accessible On & Off Campus 🌍", "B332": "All Green & Smooth 🟢 (HTTP {…}) 🎉", "B333": "Server returned status code {…} 🟠🤔", "B334": "Connection Refused by Server 🔴", "B335": "Your network adapter doesn't have a usable IP address yet 🔌—behaving just like an unplugged cable 🙈.", "B336": "Check that your Ethernet cable is clicked in snug 👉, or verify in System Settings that the adapter has a valid IP address 🛠️✨!", "B337": "No test results yet ⚪🐣.", "B338": "Click \"Start Checkup\" above 👆 to let your helper run a full scan 🩺✨!", "B339": "Woohoo! 🎉 Every single tested site got green lights across the board—your connection is in peak health 🏄‍♂️💖!", "B340": "Everything's shipshape 🏖️—nothing to fix, enjoy the smooth browsing ✨!", "B341": "Some sites failed to load 🤔, and even JLU's campus auth server (10.100.61.3) isn't answering—looks like the hiccup is right here on the local campus link 🏫💦.", "B342": "First make sure you're actually connected to the campus network 👉 (via Ethernet or JLU.PC), or grab a sip of tea and retry in a moment 🍵; if it stays quiet for a while, the university network center's auth server might be taking a maintenance nap 😴🛠️.", "B343": "Almost every unreachable site got stuck at \"DNS Lookup\" 📖: meaning domain names couldn't be translated into numeric IP addresses 🙈💦.", "B344": "Try switching your system DNS to a reliable public DNS 💡 (like 10.10.10.10 on campus or 223.5.5.5 off-campus) 🛠️; if you're running a proxy app, check its DNS settings too so queries aren't sent down a dead-end route 🕵️‍♂️✨!", "B345": "Reached the server's front door over the wire 🔒, but got rejected during the encrypted TLS handshake—meaning a middlebox is intercepting traffic, or the site's security certificate looks fishy 🚧🧐.", "B346": "If you have a proxy running, try turning it off for a second 👉📴; if the handshake still fails without a proxy, an upstream firewall or ISP filter is likely blocking the connection 🛡️💦.", "B347": "Network routing and TLS encryption both passed with flying colors 🤝! The website's own server is just having a grumpy moment and threw back an error code (4xx / 5xx) 😤.", "B348": "That usually means the website itself is under maintenance or rate-limiting traffic ☕—nothing wrong with your Mac or proxy settings. Just check back later 🏖️✨!", "B349": "Domestic sites load at warp speed 🐼, but overseas sites all timed out: your proxy app is running,yet its outbound node isn't actually carrying traffic across the border ✈️💥.", "B350": "Try switching to a fresh, lively node in your proxy app 👉🔄, or check if your proxy plan ran out of data 💸; otherwise, turn the proxy off for now and enjoy blazing-fast campus direct speeds 🏄‍♂️✨!", "B351": "Domestic sites are all green 🐼, overseas sites won't load, and no proxy app is running—haha,that's the textbook definition of a pure, unproxied campus connection 😂✨!", "B352": "Whenever you need to visit overseas sites like GitHub 💡, remember to fire up your proxy app first ✈️; for domestic and campus browsing, you're already golden 🏖️!", "B353": "Public websites work fine 🌍, but JLU internal systems ({…}) won't open—because they're shy \"Campus Intranet Only\" portals 🔒 (Note: Student Webmail works everywhere by design, so that one doesn't count ✉️😜)!", "B354": "If you're off-campus right now 🌉 (on home Wi-Fi or a phone hotspot), sign into JLU WebVPN first; if you're right here in your dorm, check whether your campus network authentication dropped offline 🔄✨!", "B355": "Several sites couldn't even complete a basic TCP connection 💥: your outbound path to the internet is cut off (either your proxy node went down, or the upstream link is unplugged 🔌💦).", "B356": "Try picking a different node in your proxy app first 👉🔄; if that still fails, turn off the proxy completely and test with a pure direct connection to see if the campus network itself is healthy 🕵️‍♂️✨.", "B357": "Double-check that your campus connection is authenticated and online 🔍—you can also hop over to the \"Details\" tab and Ping the gateway to test the local road 🏓✨.", "B358": "A handful of sites failed to load 🤔, but for a mix of different reasons rather than one single bottleneck 🧩.", "B359": "Peek at the individual results below 👇 to see where each site got stuck—then decide whether to tweak DNS, swap proxy nodes, or just blame the website's own server 🩺✨!", "B401": "Not registered yet 📭", "B402": "Unknown / Mystery ❓", "B403": "Heads up! 🪪 The campus gateway is a strict by-the-book guard that recognizes devices solely by MAC address: your current adapter{…} has the hardware address {…}, while your account profile has {…} on file 🙈! Keep in mind that Wired Ethernet uses your dongle/port's MAC, whereas JLU.PCuses your Mac's built-in Wi-Fi MAC—they're two separate pieces of hardware and can't impersonate each other 🙅‍♂️. To surf on this connection, head over to the Campus Self-Service Portal and update your registered MAC to {…} first ✍️ (Friendly note: once updated, your previously bound adapter won't be able to authenticate until you switch it back 🔄)!", "B404": "(Couldn't read hardware MAC address 🙈)", "B405": "(No registered MAC entered yet 📭)", "B406": "Caught an impostor in disguise! 🎭 macOS dressed this adapter up in a \"Private / Randomized MAC\" costume: {…} (whenever the 2nd character of the first pair is 2, 6, a, or e, it's a randomized address cooked up by the OS 🕵️‍♂️), whereas the card's true factory MAC is {…}, and your JLU registered MAC is {…}. Don't panic—we've got 3 ways to tame it 💡: 1️⃣ Best Fix 🌟: Open macOS \"System Settings ⚙️ → Network → click this adapter → Details → Hardware / Wi-Fi\" and turn off \"Private Wi-Fi Address\" so it goes back to its true factory MAC; 2️⃣ Lazy Magic 🪄: Flip on \"Authenticate with Registered MAC\" right in our app Settings (we'll sign the auth packets with your registered MAC without touching your system adapter ✨); 3️⃣ Last Resort 🙅‍♂️: Update your registered MAC on ip.jlu.edu.cn to match this random address (strongly discouraged! Next time you reconnect or switch Wi-Fi, macOS might roll a brand-new random MAC and knock you offline again 😭).", "B407": "Heads up! 📡 Connecting to JLU.PC wireless requires authenticating with your Mac's built-in Wi-Fi MAC address. If your JLU account is currently bound to a USB Ethernet dongle or wired port MAC,authentication here will hit a brick wall 🚧—head over to ip.jlu.edu.cn to update your registered MAC to this Wi-Fi card's address first ✍️ (Note: doing so will temporarily unbind your wired Ethernet port 🔄)!", "B408": "After connecting to JLU.PC 🎉, a login.jlu.edu.cn welcome page often pops up in your browser—that's just the campus landing portal (100% normal 🤗). Feel free to close that tab right away ✖️: JLU Gate already handled the real authentication quietly in the background 🛡️, so there's zero need to download the old official client from that page 🙅‍♂️✨!", "B409": "The campus server shook its head 🙅‍♂️—it doesn't recognize this MAC address under your account profile. Since a Mac's hardware MAC is permanently etched in at the factory 🛠️, please head to ip.jlu.edu.cn to verify or update your registered MAC ✍️, or plug back in the USB adapter/dock you originally registered 🔌✨!", "B410": "JLU.WIFI allows up to {…} devices online at the same time per account 📱🏄‍♂️. Whenever a new device logs in, it works like a boba shop line—bumping the earliest connected device right offline 🦵💥!Your previous session was very likely bumped off by your own phone or tablet logging in 🙈✨.", "B411": "Clicking Log In right now puts this Mac at the fresh end of the online queue 🔄 while kicking out whichever device is sitting at the front 🦵—if that happens to be a tablet or phone you're streaming a show on, its connection will drop instantly 📱💦!", "B412": "Local Heads-Up 💻: Beyond the {…}-device limit, logging in now will put this Mac at the back of the queue and take over the connection 🔄. {…}", "B413": "Fun fact 💡: That mini browser window that pops up whenever you join a new Wi-Fi is macOS's built-in \"Captive Network Assistant\" 🤖—triggered straight by the OS kernel where apps can't block it 🤷‍♂️. Just ignore it! As soon as JLU Gate finishes authenticating in the background ⚡, that window senses the live connection and closes itself automatically 👋✨!", "B501": "Not checked yet ⚪", "B502": "Just typed in manually ✍️", "B503": "Safely saved 💖 (and logged in successfully before ✌️)", "B504": "Saved 🤔 (haven't tested it live yet 🐣)", "B505": "Saved 😭 (but turned down by the server last time 💔)", "B506": "Auto Mode 🤖 (hasn't sent a scout probe yet 🕵️‍♂️)", "B507": "This Mac 💻 {…}", "B508": "Already surfing online 🎉 (even before setting up an account here 🏄‍♂️)", "B509": "To prevent back-to-back lockouts 🛡️, we stopped auto-retrying the old password—let's type a fresh one ✍️", "B510": "To avoid getting temp-blocked by the server for wrong attempts 🔑, please re-enter your correct password ✨!", "B511": "That server address format doesn't look quite right 🙈", "B512": "Opened using the portal URL we thoughtfully jotted down last time 🚀📖✨!", "B513": "Sniffing out the portal URL right now 🕵️‍♂️… ⏳", "B514": "Shadowrocket / Clash / Proxy App 🚀", "B515": "Via Default Outbound Interface 🚪", "B516": "Oops 🔌, wired adapter {…} doesn't have an IP address yet 📭. Pop in the static parameters from your registration slip (or switch the adapter to DHCP in System Settings), then let's try connecting again 🛠️✨!", "C01": "Needs a quick hand from you here 🙋‍♂️! Once sorted, hit \"Retry\" to get back to surfing 🏄‍♂️✨!", "C02": "Retry 🔄", "C03": "View Network Details 📊", "C04": "Close ✖️", "D01": "Network X-Ray & Details 📊", "D02": "Refresh 🔄", "D03": "Reading network state ⏳…", "D04": "VPN/TUN is steering traffic 🦸‍♂️", "D05": "VPN/TUN not active 🍃", "D06": "· ⚠️ DNS is being intercepted by a proxy", "D07": "Proxy Mode 🚀 (vs. Clash / Surge / Shadowrocket)", "D08": "Matches what you picked in your proxy app to a tee! ✅", "D09": "Huh 🤔, looks slightly different from what's selected in your proxy app", "D10": "Analyzing routing table 🕵️‍♂️…", "D11": "What you selected in your proxy app 👉:", "D12": "No utun virtual interface spotted 🍃: no VPN or proxy is grabbing the steering wheel (routing table) right now 🚗✨.", "D13": "Default Outbound Interface 🚪", "D14": "Auth Traffic Outbound Interface 🪪", "D15": "Wired Ethernet 🔌", "D16": "Wireless Wi-Fi 📡", "D17": "Auth Traffic 🪪", "D18": "Active 🟢", "D19": "Inactive ⚪", "D20": "True Factory MAC {…} 🏭 ← Actually used for authentication (even while macOS wears a randomized Private MAC disguise 🎭)", "D21": "Link-Local Address {…} 🔗", "D22": "No physical Ethernet adapter detected 🙈", "D23": "Routing & DNS Signposts 🧭", "D24": "Default Route 🛣️", "D25": "{…} (Next-hop gateway {…} 🦘)", "D26": "System DNS 📖", "D27": "(Couldn't read DNS 🙈)", "D28": "Your system DNS is currently 198.18.x.x 💡 (a fake-ip placeholder generated by your proxy app 🎭). No worries though—our built-in probes bypass it and fire direct UDP queries 🚀!", "D29": "Auth Channel Latency ⏱️ (UDP 61440 round-trip sprint 🏃‍♂️)", "D30": "Whether you can stay authenticated with Global Proxy on depends entirely on how smooth this path is 💡—mode labels alone don't tell the whole story 🧐! Let's fire 3 real challenge packets both directly and through your proxy to see 🎯:", "D31": "Timing with a stopwatch ⏳…", "D32": "Test Auth Channel 🏃‍♂️", "D33": "Ping Test 🏓 (TCP Handshake Latency)", "D34": "Hit \"Start Ping\" below 👇 to measure round-trip time to the campus gateway and public web—and see how much extra time VPN routing adds ⏱️✨!", "D35": "Start Ping! 🏓", "D36": "Speed Test Drag Race 🚀 (HTTP Download: Direct vs. VPN Showdown 🏎️)", "D37": "We'll download a small test chunk via both \"Physical Interface Direct\" and \"Default Outbound (with VPN)\" to compare speeds in Mbps 🏁✨.", "D38": "Direct interface speed test unavailable ⚠️: either the campus gateway blocked it 🚧, or the test server only accepts proxied traffic 🤔.", "D39": "Flooring the gas pedal 🏎️…💨", "D40": "Start Speed Test 🚀", "D41": "Copy All Info 📋", "D42": "Close ✖️", "E01": "Malformed Auth Packet 📦💥 ({…})", "E02": "Received an unrecognizable mystery packet 👽: type 0x{…}, subtype 0x{…}, length {…}", "E03": "{…} is a bit too long 📏—it can only fit up to {…} bytes 🙈", "E04": "Registered MAC Not Set 📭", "E05": "MAC Address Mismatch 🪪💥: Your JLU profile has {…} on file, but the active interface is {…} 🙈.If you switched to a new USB adapter or dock, register its MAC on the Campus Self-Service Portal first 🏫✍️!", "E06": "Interface {…} has no IPv4 address yet 📭. Head to macOS \"System Settings → Network\" and configure your assigned static campus IP first (remember: static auth won't accept temporary DHCP addresses 🙅‍♂️✨)!", "E07": "Adapter {…} suddenly unplugged or lost link 🔌💔 (did the cable wiggle loose or the dock get unplugged 🤔?). Plug it back in snug and we'll auto-reconnect in a heartbeat 🔄💖!", "E08": "Interface {…} is still coasting on automatic DHCP instead of manual static config ⚠️🛠️. JLU's static authentication is strict and rejects DHCP addresses—flip it to manual in System Settings first ✍️!", "E09": "{…} doesn't match what's on file 🧐: expected {…}, but detected {…} 💦", "E10": "Calling campus auth server {…}, but getting total radio silence 😴 (No response). Check that your cable is plugged in tight and your static IP & Gateway are typed correctly 🔍🔌!", "E11": "Caught your proxy app hijacking the campus subnet too 🚨 (current outbound is {…}) 🕳️! That sends auth packets on a wild goose chase—set 10.0.0.0/8 to DIRECT in your proxy rules, or turn off Global routing first 🛠️✨!", "E12": "The official Dr.Com client{…} is holding onto the auth channel right now 🤝 (it claimed local port 61440 first)—which usually means it already has you connected and online 🌐✨!", "E13": "Want to switch over to the lighter, smoother JLU Gate instead? 🔄 Log out and quit the official client first 👋; if the port stays locked, open Activity Monitor and quit its background helper DrClientNS🧹✨!", "E14": "Oops 📞💥, the dedicated campus auth hotline (local UDP port 61440) is already taken by another app{…} 🙈!", "E15": "Nine times out of ten, that's the official Dr.Com client 💡—quit it completely and we'll take the wheel smoothly 🚀✨!", "E16": "Looks like your current network isn't the JLU campus network 🏞️ ({…})—your little helper will stand by quietly for now 💤", "E17": "Whoops 🛠️, we haven't learned how to support this connection type yet: {…} 🙈", "E18": "Waited until the flowers wilted, but the campus server never wrote back ⏱️💔 (Timed out: {…}) 🥀", "E19": "Hit a small bump on the network channel 🚧: {…} 💦", "E20": "Operation Cancelled 🛑", "E21": "Campus Server Announcement 🔄: DHCP dynamic IP is required for this connection!", "E22": "MAC Address Verification Failed 🪪💥", "E23": "Campus Server is Swamped right now 🥵 (Sweating buckets!)", "E24": "Incorrect Password 🔑💥", "E25": "Insufficient Account Balance 💸", "E26": "Account Frozen or Suspended 🥶", "E27": "IP Address Mismatch 🏠💥", "E28": "MAC Address Mismatch 🪪💥", "E29": "Max Simultaneous Devices Reached 📱💥", "E30": "Server Rejected Login Credentials 🙅‍♂️ (Error 0x15)", "E31": "Both IP and MAC Addresses Mismatched! 💥", "E32": "Dynamic DHCP Address Required 🔄", "E33": "The network card currently in action doesn't match the one bound to your account 🪪: make sure you're using the adapter registered with JLU (and that macOS Private/Randomized Wi-Fi Address is turned off 🎭)!", "E34": "The campus auth server is packed with a huge queue right now and catching its breath 🥵! No need to touch any settings—grab a sip of water 🍵 and we'll retry for you automatically 🔄✨!", "E35": "Double-check your JLU Pass (Unified Identity Auth) password 🔑! If you recently changed your password on the web portal, remember to update it right here too ✍️✨!", "E36": "Your campus network balance has hit rock bottom 💸! Hop over to the Self-Service Portal to top up your account, and you'll be back to surfing in no time 💰🏄‍♂️!", "E37": "Your campus network account is currently frozen or suspended 🥶—you'll need to reach out to the teachers at the Big Data & Network Management Center to unfreeze it 📞🏫.", "E38": "This Mac's current IP doesn't match the static IP bound to your account 🏠: check if your Ethernet cable is plugged into the wrong dorm wall port 🔌, or if this network requires automatic DHCP instead 🤔!", "E39": "You've hit the ceiling on simultaneous online devices for your account 📱! Log out on one of your other phones or computers to free up a spot 🔄✨.", "E40": "On the JLU campus network 💡, error code 0x15 almost always means \"Wrong Password\" 🔑 (as documented by the open-source pioneers in jlu-drcom-ng 🤓);", "E41": "Though there's a tiny chance the campus server updated its protocol rules. Try signing into the web-based JLU Pass portal first to confirm your password works 🌐, then type it in fresh right here ✍️✨!", "E42": "Head over to macOS \"System Settings → Network\" 👉, switch this interface's IPv4 configuration to \"Using DHCP\", and come back to hit Retry 🔄✨!", "G01": "Using JLU.WIFI? 🎉 Eyes here: you don't need to fill in IP or MAC at all!", "G02": "Staring at these network fields in confusion? 🤔 Let's look them up on the Campus Self-Service Portal 🔍!", "G03": "JLU.WIFI uses hassle-free web login 🌐 with automatic DHCP addresses—just sign in with your JLU Pass credentials when the browser pops up 🥳!", "G04": "Double-check that the Wi-Fi name is spelled JLU.WIFI (all caps with a dot 🟢) before connecting ⚠️—never type your password into a sketchy lookalike network 🛡️!", "G05": "Pro tip 💡: Static IP and Gateway live under \"Query Info\" (查询信息), while your Registered MAC is under \"Change MAC\" (变更 MAC). Still can't connect? Your campus net balance might be running on fumes 💸!", "G06": "Portal Shortcut 🌐: Open ip.jlu.edu.cn/pay 🚀", "G07": "Collapse card 🔼", "G08": "Show step-by-step guide 📖", "G09": "1️⃣ Connect to JLU.WIFI first (exact spelling counts!), then click our menu bar icon → hit \"Log In\" 🚀,", "G10": "2️⃣ Type your JLU Pass username and password into the web page that pops up, and you're in ✌️✨!", "G11": "Zero need to touch IP / Mask / Gateway / MAC 🎈—addresses are handed out automatically, and web login only cares about your account 😎!", "G12": "The Self-Service Portal is your go-to spot for checking balances 💰, activating your network account 📝, or seeing which devices are currently online 👀.", "G13": "To log in there 🔑, use: Campus Card Number (the long ID on your admission letter, e.g.,20220501324) + 6-digit numeric PIN + captcha 🔢✨.", "G14": "Once inside, click \"Query Info\" (查询信息) 🔍: your IP, Gateway, and DNS are all lined up right there—though your MAC address lives next door 🙅‍♂️.", "G15": "Want to view or update your Registered MAC? 🪪 Click \"Change MAC\" (变更 MAC) right beside it to check or edit ✍️✨!", "G16": "List looking completely empty with no IP? 😮 Head back to the main menu and hit \"Activate Network\" (网络开户) 🎉 first, then check again!", "G17": "Demystifying the \"Three Campus Passwords\" Once and For All! 🤯", "G18": "How do I find my Mac's MAC address? 💻", "G19": "Friendly reminder 💡: If you're connecting to JLU.WIFI, skip all these static fields! It runs on dynamic addresses and web authentication 🏖️✨.", "G20": "1. JLU V-Card (Campus Card) 💳", "G21": "Username = Admission Letter ID; Password = 6-digit PIN 🔢. Use this combo on the Campus Network Self-Service Portal to check info and top up your balance 💰!", "G22": "2. JLU Email 📧", "G23": "Has its own separate password 🔒 strictly for checking campus webmail ✉️—though the username prefix before @ is identical to your JLU Pass ✨.", "G24": "3. JLU Pass / Unified Identity Auth (Most Used 🌟) 🔑", "G25": "Course registration, WebVPN, and right here in JLU Gate (including JLU.WIFI web login) all run on this master account and password 👑✨!", "G26": "Finding your Wired Ethernet MAC 🔌:", "G27": "Open macOS \"System Settings\" ⚙️ → \"Network\" 🌐 → click your plugged-in Ethernet adapter (USB dongles show up here too!) → \"Details\" → \"Hardware\", and boom, there's your \"MAC Address\" 👀✨!", "G28": "Finding your Wi-Fi MAC 📡: Open \"System Settings\" ⚙️ → \"Wi-Fi\" → click \"Details…\" next to your connected campus Wi-Fi (JLU.WIFI / JLU.PC) → \"Hardware\" to spot your MAC 🎯!", "G29": "Make sure you grab the adapter's real factory hardware address ⚠️! If macOS is being overly protective with \"Private Wi-Fi Address\" (randomized MAC) turned on 🎭,", "G30": "remember to switch it off 🙅‍♂️, or simply check \"Authenticate with Registered MAC\" in our app Settings 🪄✨!", "G31": "Still can't connect no matter what? 💸 Check your wallet—your account might be overdue 🙈", "G32": "The campus network is pretty forgiving and lets you surf even at -10 RMB or 0 RMB 🏄‍♂️; but once your balance hits -20 RMB, it pulls the plug ✂️ (across Wired, JLU.PC, and JLU.WIFI alike).", "G33": "Top-ups only come in 20 / 40 / 100 RMB tiers 💰, deducted straight from your Campus Card.Heads up! If you owe 20 RMB, topping up just 20 RMB brings you to 0 RMB—which won't restore your connection 😱!", "G34": "You'll need to top up 40 RMB in one go so your balance lands in positive territory (+20 RMB) before the network welcomes you back with open arms 🤗✨!", "G35": "You can check all your balances and bills under \"Query Info\" on the Self-Service Portal 🔍 using your Campus Card number + 6-digit V-Card PIN 👀.", "G36": "Open Self-Service Portal to take a look 🚀", "G37": "Must-Read Freshman Tips 🌱✨", "G38": "📸 When you move to another dorm, the school may show a \"User Migration\" page listing the adapter's physical address (MAC), the old IP and the new IP—take a screenshot and keep it 📷. You'll need those numbers when filling in the network parameters and registering the MAC on the Self-Service Portal.", "M01": "Yay! 🎉 No web login needed right now—enjoy the smooth sailing 🏖️✨", "M02": "Go back 🔙", "M03": "Oops, we need a quick hand here 🙋‍♂️! Once you've sorted it out, just hit \"Retry\" 🔄✨!", "M04": "Connection path 🌐", "M05": "Local IP 🏠", "M06": "The exclusive digital door number JLU assigned to your Mac 🪧✨", "M07": "Rock-solid online 🟢", "M08": "Your little helper is quietly keeping your session alive in the background 💓—just sit back and relax ☕️✨!", "M09": "Outbound interface 🚪", "M10": "Which network card your login packets slip out from 🏃‍♂️. Going through a proxy isn't always bad,but if it lags or drops packets 🐢, the campus server might think you've disconnected 🥺.", "M11": "Plugged in via Ethernet 🔌—rock solid as a mountain ⛰️✨!", "M12": "Campus Wi-Fi signal 📡—needs your Wi-Fi card's identity to swipe in and authenticate 🪪✨", "M13": "Web Portal login 🌐—time to call in your browser 🧭✨!", "M14": "Auto Mode 🤖: Scouting the path ahead 🕵️‍♂️ to pick the smoothest way online for you ✨!", "M15": "Since {…} ⏰ · Keeping you company for {…} ✨", "M16": "Fill in your account & password ✍️ (we'll auto-reconnect in a heartbeat if the line ever drops 🔄💓)", "M17": "Heading out 👋 (Disconnect)", "M18": "Let's gooo! 🚀 Log In!", "M19": "Give it another shot 🔄", "M20": "Re-enter password 🔑", "M21": "Whoops, your proxy grabbed the campus subnet too 🚧! Let's add a quick direct-route shortcut first 🛣️:", "M22": "Copy magic command 📋", "M23": "I ran the command 🙋‍♂️—check again!", "M24": "JLU.WIFI only lets up to {…} devices stay online at the same time 📱👯‍♂️", "M25": "Reclaim my online spot! 🤺", "M26": "Open Web Login page 🌐", "M27": "Run setup again 🛠️…", "M28": "Switch to factory MAC {…} 🏭✨", "M29": "Open Self-Service Portal 🏫 (to update registered MAC ✍️)", "M30": "Only one device per account can be online at a time ☝️. Want this Mac online? Log out on your other device (or grab a sip of tea and wait 30 seconds for auto-release 🍵), then hit Retry 🔄!", "M31": "Huh? Another device already claimed this MAC address 😱! If you swapped adapters or use a shared budget dongle, head over to the campus portal to double-check your registered info 🔍🏫!", "M32": "Settings ⚙️", "M33": "Campus Links 🧭", "M34": "Details 📊", "M35": "Diagnostics 🩺", "M36": "Health Check 🏥", "M37": "Quit 🚪", "M38": "Updates 🌟: Check GitHub for a fresh release 📦", "M39": "Hunting for the latest version 🔍… ⏳", "M40": "Woohoo! You're already rocking the latest and greatest version v{…} 🎉✨!", "M41": "Ding-dong! 🔔 New version {…} spotted: click \"Update\" to auto-download and slip into the new build 👗✨!", "M42": "Update Now ⬆️", "M43": "Taking a peek ⏳…", "M44": "Check again 🔄", "N01": "Disconnect 👋", "N02": "Connect Now 🚀", "N03": "Refresh Status 🔄", "N04": "Network Health Check 🏥", "N05": "Settings ⚙️…", "N06": "Quit JLU Gate 🚪", "N07": "Screen width {…}, center line {…} 📏", "N08": "Reset icon position preference to default 🧹", "N09": "Whoops 👈, the menu bar icon drifted over to the left side of the screen", "N10": "About JLU Gate 💖", "N11": "Quietly keeping your JLU campus connection rock-solid 24/7 🛡️✨", "N12": "Woohoo! 🎉 Successfully updated to the latest version!", "N13": "The old version (build {…}) has retired with honors 👋—brand-new build {…} is now at your service 🚀✨!", "N14": "JLU Gate needs a quick hand from you 🙋‍♂️", "N15": "Looks like the app isn't living in your /Applications folder yet 📦, so we can't auto-replace it for updates 🥺. Drag JLU Gate into /Applications first to enjoy seamless one-click updates 🏠✨!", "N16": "Download failed 😭: {…}", "N17": "Unpacking failed 📦💥: {…}", "N18": "Downloading the new version 📥… ⏳", "N19": "Unpacking the archive 📦… ✨", "N20": "Huh 🤔? Couldn't find a .app bundle inside the downloaded archive", "N21": "Retiring the old version and slipping into the new build 🔄… 👗✨", "N22": "(Newer than the version you're currently running! 🌟)", "N23": "(Older than your current version—feel free to trash it and save some disk space 🍂🗑️)", "N24": "⚠️ JLUGate: Tripped while writing to log file {…}", "N25": "🎒 JLUGate: Portable copies running outside /Applications won't register as login items ✨", "N26": "⚠️ JLUGate: Failed to configure Launch at Login item {…}", "P01": "This checkup inspects the exact path your browser takes online 🩺: where your outbound IP lands,whether WebRTC spills your real IP, if DNS is wandering off, and whether annoying CAPTCHAs load properly 🧩✨.", "P02": "Can You Actually Surf Smoothly? 🌐 (Including JLU Internal Portals 🏫)", "P03": "Your checkup starts automatically the moment you open this tab ✨; use the button below anytime you want a fresh re-run 🔄!", "P04": "JLU Internal Portals 🏫 (Academic & OA notices work on-campus only 🔒; Student Webmail works everywhere ✉️✨)", "P05": "Running a thorough checkup 🩺… ⏳", "P06": "Run Checkup Again 🔄", "P07": "Outbound IP 🚪", "P08": "CAPTCHA Verification 🤖", "P09": "(Bilibili 📺 cleverly took a split-tunnel side road 🛤️)", "P10": "Huh ⚠️, different detectors report different countries ({…})—this is likely an anycast/broadcast IP or a relay node 📡✨", "P100": "Japan 🇯🇵", "P101": "South Korea 🇰🇷", "P102": "South Korea 🇰🇷", "P103": "Singapore 🇸🇬", "P104": "United States 🇺🇸", "P105": "Hong Kong SAR 🇭🇰", "P106": "Taiwan 🇹🇼", "P107": "United Kingdom 🇬🇧", "P108": "Germany 🇩🇪", "P109": "Russia 🇷🇺", "P11": "DNS & Outbound IP Harmony 🧭:", "P110": "Canada 🇨🇦", "P111": "Australia 🇦🇺", "P112": "Netherlands 🇳🇱", "P113": "France 🇫🇷", "P114": "Couldn't fetch a DNS exit address 🙈 (your proxy might have locked down DNS, or the query timed out), so we can't compare them this round 🤷‍♂️.", "P115": "System DNS is currently managed by your proxy app 🎭 (resolving to the Fake-IP placeholder {…}),", "P116": "so its real physical exit stays hidden behind the curtain—don't worry, that's not a leak or mismatch, just an invisibility cloak at work 🧥✨!", "P117": "Picture perfect! 🌟 Your DNS resolver exit and your outbound IP are the exact same address—making you look 100% like a natural local user to website security checks 🏡💖!", "P118": "Missing country geolocation data 🤔, so we can't run a comparison just yet 🕵️‍♂️.", "P119": "Your DNS exit ({…}) and IP exit ({…}) are in the exact same country/region ✅—marching in lockstep with very low risk of triggering anti-bot alarms 👍✨!", "P12": "3-Way Bandwidth Showdown 🏎️", "P120": "Heads up! 🚨 Your DNS queries are popping out in {…}, while your actual traffic exits worlds away in {…} 🌍💦—", "P121": "This \"split-brain\" routing is the #1 giveaway that tips off strict security systems 👀, sometimes triggering blocks or CAPTCHAs even faster than a datacenter IP 😱!", "P13": "Pure Direct 🛣️", "P14": "Default Outbound (w/ Proxy) 🚪", "P15": "Local Proxy Port 💻", "P16": "Local Proxy 127.0.0.1:7890 💻", "P17": "Burning rubber on the speed test 🏎️… 💨", "P18": "Test Speed 🚀", "P19": "No local proxy port detected 💡: if you're running TUN virtual adapter mode, Tier 2 already shows your final proxied speed—no need to test Tier 3 ✌️✨!", "P20": "Auto-detected local proxy port {…} ({…}) 🎯! Feel free to edit it manually if needed ✍️!", "P21": "Open Campus Portal in browser 🌐", "P22": "Residential / Native ISP IP 🏡: The absolute favorite of picky streaming and AI sites like Claude and Netflix 💖✨!", "P23": "Datacenter / Hosting IP 🏢: Strict websites might give it the cold shoulder 🙅‍♂️ or bombard you with endless CAPTCHA puzzles 🧩💦", "P24": "Mobile Cellular IP 📱: Usually behaves great 👍, though bandwidth might get throttled during peak hours 🐢", "P25": "Not enough ASN database info to tell what flavor of IP this is yet 🤔🕵️‍♂️", "P26": "Click \"Start Check\" above 👆 and we'll look up this outbound IP's background and type (cozy residential home 🏡 vs. server farm 🏢) ✨", "P27": "Knocking on doors across the web asking 🗣️: \"Hey, who am I and where am I coming from in your eyes?\"… 🔍", "P28": "Click \"Start Check\" 👆 to ask several major websites the exact same philosophical question 🧐✨", "P29": "Outbound IP Reputation & Purity Test 🧼", "P30": "Uh-oh 🚨, flagged as a proxy IP on public blocklists", "P31": "Geolocation 📍", "P32": "Carrier / ASN 🏷️", "P33": "IP Type 🧬", "P34": "· 🏢 Tagged as Datacenter / Hosting", "P35": "Other Supporting Clues 🔍", "P36": "Haven't checked yet ⚪", "P37": "Region 🌍: {…}", "P38": "Edge Datacenter 🏢: {…}", "P39": "See which country and edge datacenter cyber-guardian Cloudflare thinks you're popping out from 👀🕵️‍♂️", "P40": "Cloudflare is one of the sharpest judges of where traffic originates 💡—the closer the edge datacenter you hit, the snappier your browsing usually feels 🏄‍♂️✨!", "P41": "No response received 📭 ({…})", "P42": "STUN is the whisper protocol browsers use via WebRTC to ask \"What's my real public IP?\" 📡—let's run the exact same probe right now 🕵️‍♂️✨!", "P43": "What's a \"DNS Leak\"? 💡 It's when your traffic puts on a proxy invisibility cloak 🧥, but your Mac still asks your local ISP to look up domain names—giving away where you're browsing from 🙈!", "P44": "Also spotted suspicious DNS hijacking signs ⚠️ (even a totally made-up gibberish domain returned an IP address 👻)!", "P45": "Awesome! ✅ Your System DNS and Public DNS exit from the exact same region ({…}) 🎉", "P46": "Hmm 🤔, System DNS exits in {…}, while Public DNS exits in {…}—they're taking two separate routes for domain lookups 🛤️!", "P47": "System DNS exits in {…} 📍; Public DNS couldn't be reached (either blocked 🚧 or fully intercepted by your proxy app 🦸‍♂️).", "P48": "No reply from System DNS 📭; however, Public DNS exits in {…} ✨.", "P49": "Yikes 😱, neither DNS test got a receipt—your entire DNS query channel might be blocked or intercepted 🚧!", "P50": "Reachable & Smooth 🟢", "P51": "Unreachable 🔴", "P52": "Triggers CAPTCHA Challenge 🟡🧩", "P53": "Returned unexpected/weird content 🟠👽", "P54": "Outbound IP matches your local campus IP 🏠: traffic went straight out via direct connection without entering a proxy tunnel 🍃!", "P55": "Outbound region is in {…} ✈️: traffic hopped aboard your proxy plane and exited through an overseas/remote node 🌍✨!", "P56": "Outbound IP differs from your local address 🔀", "P57": "No STUN reply received 🛡️: UDP traffic is likely blocked tight (silver lining: WebRTC definitely won't leak your real IP this way ✌️✨)!", "P58": "Heads up! 🚨 STUN spotted your real local IP {…} right away—meaning browser WebRTC could expose your true address to websites 🙈!", "P59": "STUN sees {…} 👀: this is the public face your browser shows the world over WebRTC 🎭.", "P60": "Not tested yet ⚪🐣", "P61": "None of the CAPTCHA providers loaded 😭: when visiting overseas sites, verification checkboxes might just spin forever 🧩💦.", "P62": "{…} sites threw a CAPTCHA wall right away 😅: looks like your current outbound node is getting extra scrutiny from anti-bot systems 🚨!", "P63": "Every single one loaded smoothly! 🎉 Your current IP has a squeaky-clean reputation right now ✌️✨!", "P64": "{…}/{…} reachable 📊, with {…} currently unreachable 🤔", "P65": "Interface Name 🔌 (e.g., en0 / en7)", "P66": "macOS's internal nickname for each network adapter 🏷️. Plugging a USB dongle into a different port can change this name 🎭—so we always identify your card by its permanent MAC address instead 🎯!", "P67": "MAC Address (Physical Address) 🪪", "P68": "The unique hardware ID etched into your network card at the factory 🏭. JLU's gateway recognizes your device strictly by MAC—if you swap USB adapters or borrow a dock 🔄, remember to update your registered MAC on the Self-Service Portal first 🚧!", "P69": "IPv4 Address 🏠", "P70": "Your Mac's personal street number on the JLU campus network 🪧. Because JLU assigns fixed IPs by dorm wall port, you must copy it straight from your registration slip 📝—DHCP auto-addresses won't cut it 🙅‍♂️!", "P71": "Subnet Mask 🎭", "P72": "Draws the boundary between \"our dorm building\" and \"the rest of the world\" 📏. If mistyped, your Mac treats the building gateway like a stranger and refuses to talk to it 🙈!", "P73": "Default Gateway 🚪", "P74": "The very first hop your packets take out of the dorm building 🦘 (the floor/building router). It must sit on the same subnet as your IP, or your packets will shout into the void with no one answering 📣💦!", "P75": "DNS (Domain Name System) 📖: Translates human-friendly web addresses (like jlu.edu.cn) into numeric IP addresses 🔢. When intercepted by a proxy app, domains often resolve to temporary 198.18.x.x fake-ip addresses first 🎭.", "P76": "Link-Local Address (169.254.x.x) 🔗", "P77": "A makeshift \"camping tent\" IP your adapter gives itself before getting an official address ⛺.Dr.Com login packets are picky and ask to include it anyway (or 0 if none exists) ✨.", "P78": "Route / Outbound Interface 🧭", "P79": "Decides which network door your packets walk out of 🚪. If traffic heading to the campus auth server (10.100.61.3) gets routed into a utun virtual adapter 🕳️, your proxy hijacked the auth packet and it probably won't reach the campus gateway 🚨!", "P80": "utun (Virtual Tunnel Adapter) 🚇: A virtual network card conjured up by proxy apps like Clash,Surge, Shadowrocket, or WireGuard 🪄. Once it grabs the default route, all traffic dives into the tunnel first—which is why we set the campus subnet (10.0.0.0/8) to DIRECT in proxy rules 🛣️✨!", "P81": "Wireless 📡 / Wired 🔌", "P82": "Picks which physical lane carries your auth packets 🛤️. Wired Ethernet and JLU.PC share the same static IP parameters and credentials 💳, while JLU.WIFI runs on breezy dynamic web authentication 🌐✨.", "P83": "Speed Unit (Mbps) 🚀", "P84": "Quick nerd fact 🤓: lowercase b (megabits) and uppercase B (megabytes) differ by a factor of 8 (1 Byte = 8 bits)! A \"100M broadband\" plan means 100 Mbps—divide by 8 to get the actual 12.5 MB/sdownload speed you see in apps 🧮✨!", "P85": "Ping Latency (ms) 🏓", "P86": "How many milliseconds a packet takes for a round trip ⏱️. Inside the campus network, it's usually under 10ms—lightning fast ⚡! Routing through a remote VPN adds noticeable travel time 🐢, and packet loss means the road is bumpy 🎢.", "P87": "{…}: Timed out completely 😭 ({…}% packet loss 💔)", "P88": "%@ 📊: avg %.0f ms (min %.0f / max %.0f, %.0f%% loss ✨)", "P89": "Residential / Native ISP IP 🏡", "P90": "Datacenter IP 🏢 (Public Cloud / Hosting)", "P91": "Mobile Cellular IP 📱", "P92": "Mystery / Unknown Type ❓", "P93": "· 🚨 Flagged as Proxy", "P94": "Datacenter IP heads-up 🏢: Strict sites like Claude, online banking, or streaming platforms are much more likely to block access or throw verification walls 😭💦", "P95": "Public fraud-prevention databases have already jotted this IP down in their little black book as a proxy or VPN exit 🚨📝", "P96": "Huh 🤔, the IP's registered country ({…}) doesn't match the Cloudflare datacenter country ({…})—this is almost certainly an anycast IP or transit relay line 📡!", "P97": "Outbound IP is still inside Mainland China 🇨🇳: geo-restricted overseas sites will likely turn you away at the door 🚧", "P98": "China 🇨🇳", "P99": "Mainland China 🇨🇳", "R01": "🌙 Power in your dorm cuts off in {…} min (Sun–Thu, lights out at 23:30). Save your files 💾, plug in your phone 🔌, brush your teeth and dive under the covers 😴💤", "R02": "😴 Only {…} min until the power goes out! Save, lights off, lie down—good night, sweet dreams 🌙✨", "R03": "🎉 No power cut on Fri/Sat nights, so you can play a little longer—but don't stay up too late, and charge your phone 🔌🌙", "R04": "🌙 Lights are out already—your screen glow is bugging your roommate 👀 Get some rest, tomorrow comes early 😴💤", "R05": "☀️ 8 AM class time! Get up, wash up, grab a warm breakfast on the way 🥐—go crush today 🏃‍♂️✨", "R06": "🛌 No 8 AM class this morning—sleep in and enjoy it! Breakfast is still a good idea though 🥐😴✨", "R07": "🔔 School's out! You made it through today's classes—grab something warm at the dining hall 🍜 or lie down for a bit 🛌, you've earned it ✨", "R08": "🧰 Network diagnostics", "R09": "🪪 Campus card (physical)", "R10": "Handed out at orientation—no need to buy one. It's your key to hot water in the bathhouse and the library gates. If you lose it, you'll have to pay for a replacement offline 💸", "R11": "📱 SIM card (not the same thing!)", "R12": "At the start of term, carriers pitch a \"campus card\" plan—it has nothing to do with the school's physical card, it's just marketing. Decide by your own data needs; if you already have enough data, you don't need it at all. Never mandatory.", "R13": "🌐 Campus network (paid, but optional)", "R14": "20 CNY/month, usually 100 CNY per semester. It gets you Wi-Fi on every campus and wired access in the dorms. Not mandatory, but a few campus sites only open from inside the campus network.", "R15": "🎒 Freshman tips", "S01": "Beginner's Guide 🌱 / First time here? Read me!", "S02": "Account 👤", "S03": "JLU email prefix 📧 (e.g., zhangcyy2122 or zhangshanwu ✨)", "S04": "Password 🔐 (Safely locked in Keychain 🛡️)", "S05": "Leave blank = keep using your saved password ({…}) 💖", "S06": "Connection & Link Settings 🛤️", "S07": "Connection Mode 🚪", "S08": "Auto-Detect 🤖", "S09": "Wired Ethernet 🔌", "S10": "Double-check the exact Wi-Fi name 👀: JLU.PC / JLU.WIFI (all caps with a dot in the middle 🟢);", "S11": "Stay sharp around lookalike Wi-Fi names ⚠️—make sure it's legit before typing your campus credentials 🛡️!", "S12": "Under-the-Hood Engine 🚀", "S13": "BSD 🦅 (Default favorite—closest to the official client's native behavior ✨)", "S14": "NW 🍎 (Apple's modern Network.framework)", "S15": "Geek note 🤓: BSD uses raw sockets to pinpoint source port 61440 and bind directly to your chosen interface (IP_BOUND_IF) 🎯;", "S16": "NW routes through Apple's Network.framework 🍎 and plays by system path rules. Both send the exact same UDP packets 📦—", "S17": "Stick with BSD for everyday use 👍, and flip to NW if macOS ever gets fussy with permissions 🔄!", "S18": "Static Network Parameters 📌 (Only needed for Wired / JLU.PC 🛠️)", "S19": "You're on JLU.WIFI right now 🎉: dynamic IP + browser login means you can completely ignore all the static fields below 🏖️!", "S20": "Your assigned static IP 📝—copy it straight from your registration slip (don't use a DHCP-assigned address 🙅‍♂️)", "S21": "Subnet Mask 🎭", "S22": "255.255.255.0 is almost always a safe bet ✨", "S23": "Gateway 🚪", "S24": "First hop on your subnet 🦘, usually x.x.x.254", "S25": "Use 10.10.10.10 on campus 🏫; switch to 223.5.5.5 when off-campus 🌐✨", "S26": "Registered MAC 🪪", "S27": "The real hardware MAC address registered with JLU (not a randomized private MAC 🕵️‍♂️)", "S28": "Compatibility Mode 🐢: Turn off fancy liquid-glass visual effects (runs smoother on VMs or older GPUs; restart app to apply 🔄✨)", "S29": "Spoof Registered MAC in auth packets when macOS Private Wi-Fi Address is on 🎭 (Advanced magic 🪄)", "S30": "This only signs the auth packet with your registered MAC ✉️ without touching your network card.Still, turning off \"Private Wi-Fi Address\" in System Settings is the most foolproof route 👍✨!", "S31": "Static Network Parameters 📋", "S32": "Current System Readings 👀 (for reference & double-checking only)", "S33": "Route 🧭: {…